              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p108-q69-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Equate squared distances from the centre to the three points to find ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "(h,k)=(2,-1)",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", then ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "r^2=25",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let the centre be $(h,k)$. The three points have equal distances from the centre.\n\nComparing $(2,4)$ and $(7,-1)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(2-h)^2+(4-k)^2&=(7-h)^2+(-1-k)^2\\\\h^2+k^2-4h-8k+20&=h^2+k^2-14h+2k+50\\\\10h-10k&=30\\\\h-k&=3\\end{align*}$$\nComparing $(2,4)$ and $(-2,2)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(2-h)^2+(4-k)^2&=(-2-h)^2+(2-k)^2\\\\h^2+k^2-4h-8k+20&=h^2+k^2+4h-4k+8\\\\8h+4k&=12\\\\2h+k&=3\\end{align*}$$\nAdding the two simplified equations, then substituting into $h-k=3$:\n$$\\begin{align*}3h&=6\\\\h&=2\\\\2-k&=3\\\\k&=-1\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $(2,4)$ to find the squared radius:\n$$\\begin{align*}r^2&=(2-2)^2+(4+1)^2\\\\r^2&=25\\end{align*}$$\nThe equation is\n$$(x-2)^2+(y+1)^2=25.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
